Tim wrote:

> Would someone please tell me how to find the CPU serial number. It is
> not marked anywhere on the CPU. Show dev does not have it. The system
> is running Tru64 v5.0A. I need the serial number to obtain an OpenVMS
> Hobbyist license.

It is on the back of the chassis, on the outside.   On my XP1000
the tag is about 3/8" high and 3" long.   Besides the voltage
rating, it also has the model and serial number.   It will start
with two letters indicating the plant it was built at, followed
by a string of digits.   The first digit is the year it was built
(e.g. 9 = 1999).

For some reason, mine has a second (larger) sticker that also says
"S/N" with an alphanumeric string and a bar code.   I'm not sure
which one Compaq considered to be the "real" serial number, but
the guys at the hobbyist program don't care.

Alan



