I didn't see a problem that needed to be fixed. I assume, though, that
what you really meant to ask was "how do I copy this without filling
the disk"? About 20 years ago when I first ran into this problem on
Xenix I wrote a program that worked like "cpio -p" that I called
"copyto" that took care of this problem as well as recovering as much
as was possible from files containing bad blocks (back then disks
weren't quite so reliable as they are now).

Now, however, you can do better... gnu tar* has an option (-S) for
handling sparse files efficiently.

