     The AlphaServer firmware release notes DO NOT state the required
version of an OS for a given Hardware Platform. The table you are pointing
to only states the Minimum revision of the firmware disk that is required
for a given OS version. In the case of Tru64 UNIX V4.0F the minimum FW Disk
level is V5.4.

  The minimum version of the OS is stated in the QuickSPEC and on the
supported options web page, see url below.

http://h18002.www1.hp.com/alphaserver/options/asDS25/asDS25_options.html

from that web page

  a.. For Linux:
    a.. Minimum Operating System version for Linux is RH7.1.
    b.. Minimum Kernel Required: 2.2.17
  a.. For UNIX:
    a.. Minimum Operating System version for Tru64 UNIX is v5.1A with Patch
Kit 2: T64V51AB02AS0002-20020513.tar and NHD5. See most up-to-date patch
information.
  a.. For VMS:
    a.. Minimum Operating System version for OpenVMS is v7.3-1.
    b.. Minimum FIS: BP-RT6N0-01 rev A01 - FISK VMS 7.31 R01 CDKIT AUG02
    c.. OpenVMS clusters assumed supported unless otherwise noted.

    Reference the OpenVMS Cluster Software (SPD.78.14) for details regarding
SCSI OpenVMS Cluster system support.
    d.. MOP boot support on-board gigabit Ethernet devices not supported.
    e.. v7.3-1:
      a.. The following TIMA Kits are required. See most up-to-date patch
information.
      o VMS731_CPU2208-V0100
      o VMS731_FIBRE_SCSI-V0100
      o VMS731_SYS-V0200
      o VMS731_RMS-V0200
      o VMS731_EV7-V0100
      o DNVOSIECO01-V0703
      o TCPIP_ECO V5.3-181
      o VMS731_CPU2308-V0100

