I am trying to use the Media Robot Utility with a Dell
LTO PV132T library:

# uname -rv
V5.1 1885
# robot show version
Media Robot Utility V1.6
# robot show slot 0 robot /dev/changer/mc0
ROBOT /dev/changer/mc0 is not responding: Robot Illegal request.

I suspect the problem relates to the dbd bit not being set.
In scu, for example:

# scu -f /dev/changer/mc0
scu> show elem slot 0
scu: 'mode sense (6)' failed on device 'PV-132T' at nexus [2/0/0]
scu: Sense Key = 0x5 = ILLEGAL REQUEST - Illegal request or CDB parameter,
     Sense Code/Qualifier = (0x24, 0) = Invalid field in CDB
scu: 'mode sense (6)' failed on device 'PV-132T' at nexus [2/0/0]
scu: Sense Key = 0x5 = ILLEGAL REQUEST - Illegal request or CDB parameter,
     Sense Code/Qualifier = (0x24, 0) = Invalid field in CDB

               Element  Transport  Exception  Element
               Address   Status      State     Type
               -------  ---------  ---------  -------
Segmentation fault (core dumped)

However setting the bit fixes the problem:

# scu -f /dev/changer/mc0
scu> set default dbd 1
scu> show elem slot 0

               Element  Transport  Exception  Element
               Address   Status      State     Type
               -------  ---------  ---------  -------
       Slot 0:   4096      Empty     Normal    Storage

Is there any way to make MRU do similar? as it is a bit of a pain
having to use scu to move media around.

BTW, MRU works fine with this library under OpenVMS 7.3-1

Many thanks.


